        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Updates for Chrome 153 beta]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30300</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30300"/>
        <updated>2026-08-21T15:49:27.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/349114?u=1185d4fc45f5ff4c4a592b30a4dd2bb5cd1b7128&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><p dir="auto">The <a href="https://collector.openwebdocs.org/" rel="nofollow">https://collector.openwebdocs.org/</a> project (v10.20.7) found new features shipping in Chromium 153 beta which was released yesterday. Currently, the collector covers about 90% of BCD, so the following list might not be exhaustive. Also, if a feature is in Canary/behind flags, it is not considered here.</p>
<p dir="auto">With this PR, BCD will consider the following features as shipping in Chromium 153 (<strong>bold</strong> features are new keys in BCD).</p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li><strong>api.BaseAudioContext.renderQuantumSize</strong> (<a href="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8242387" rel="nofollow">ref</a>)</li>
<li>api.Document.browsingTopics (removal) (<a href="https://chromestatus.com/feature/5194473869017088" rel="nofollow">ref</a>)</li>
<li>api.HTMLElement.autocorrect (152-&gt;153) (<a href="https://chromiumdash.appspot.com/commits?commit=25a6eb59d05e8188b8328bc4765c1abbf2c14ae0&amp;platform=Android" rel="nofollow">ref</a>)</li>
<li>api.HTMLIFrameElement.browsingTopics (removal) (<a href="https://chromestatus.com/feature/5194473869017088" rel="nofollow">ref</a>)</li>
<li><strong>css.properties.scroll-axis-lock</strong> (<a href="https://chromestatus.com/feature/5908461532610560" rel="nofollow">ref</a>)</li>
<li><strong>css.properties.scroll-axis-lock.auto</strong> (<a href="https://chromestatus.com/feature/5908461532610560" rel="nofollow">ref</a>)</li>
<li><strong>css.properties.scroll-axis-lock.none</strong> (<a href="https://chromestatus.com/feature/5908461532610560" rel="nofollow">ref</a>)</li>
<li>javascript.builtins.Iterator.join (<a href="https://chromestatus.com/feature/5095183554314240" rel="nofollow">ref</a>)</li>
<li>javascript.builtins.Iterator.zip (<a href="https://chromestatus.com/feature/6249068542164992" rel="nofollow">ref</a>)</li>
<li>javascript.builtins.Iterator.zipKeyed (<a href="https://chromestatus.com/feature/6249068542164992" rel="nofollow">ref</a>)</li>
</ul>
<p dir="auto">See also <a href="https://developer.chrome.com/blog/chrome-153-beta" rel="nofollow">https://developer.chrome.com/blog/chrome-153-beta</a> and <a href="https://chromestatus.com/roadmap" rel="nofollow">https://chromestatus.com/roadmap</a></p>
<p dir="auto"><strong>Note</strong>: There are also new capability elements: <code class="notranslate">&lt;camera&gt;</code> and <code class="notranslate">&lt;microphone&gt;</code>, however, they are not in a spec which is considered by browser-specs, see <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="3108085776" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/w3c/browser-specs/issues/1915" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/w3c/browser-specs/issues/1915/hovercard" href="https://github.com/w3c/browser-specs/issues/1915">w3c/browser-specs#1915</a>. I will follow-up on these separately.</p>]]></content>
